WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.780
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar, and you're watching Mind Your Decisions.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:11.670
Here's a fun geometry problem. In the following shape, each of the small squares has a side length of one.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.770
The challenge is to figure out the area of this red shape.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.740
Can you figure it out?

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:24.209
Give this problem a try, and when you're ready, keep watching the video for a solution.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:44.009
So the key principle in solving this problem is to know the formula for the area of a triangle,

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.980
which is one-half its base times its height.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.959
This is true, even if the triangle is not a right angle triangle.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:59.400
All of the following triangles have the same area. It only depends on the base and the height of the triangle.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.000
So how can we figure out the area of the shape?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.900
What we'll do is we'll decompose it into two different triangles.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:15.820
First, we'll have this upper triangle, and then we'll have a lower triangle. So let's figure out the area of each of these triangles.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.390
Now this triangle has a base of 2 and a height of 2.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:25.859
So its area will be 2 times 2 all over 2, which is 2.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.930
Now let's calculate the area of this lower triangle.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:39.260
This has a base of 3 and a height of 1 so it's area will be equal to 3 times 1 over 2,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.300
which is equal to 1.5.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.280
The red shape is equal to the area of these two triangles

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.740
So its area will be equal to 3.5. And that's the answer!

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:55.890
Now just as a little bit of fun trivia, the entire shape has a total area of 7.

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:02.008
Hence, the red area is exactly half of the total area. Did you figure it out?

